      <div class="find"><b>Page n2</b><br>The next feature of popular science texts is the use of nouns in the common case as prepositive attributes. Thanks to the use of a multicomponent phrase, the authors of scientific works can convey more information with a small number of grammatical means. In addition, the above constructions have a term-forming function. For example: “excessive daytime sleepiness” - excessive daytime sleepiness [9]; <mark>artificial intelligence</mark> - <mark>artificial intelligence</mark> [6].</div>
